Hacking AptFs
=============

Automatically pruning source packages
-------------------------------------

From `mount.aptfs --help`:

    [...]
    -o max_unpackaged_packages=NUM
                           keep NUM packages unpacked at any one time
                           [default: 5]
    [...]

AptFs maintains a sliding window of unpacked sources packages -- it would not
be very helpful if commands such as:

 % find /path/to/aptfs

unpacked the entire APT archive into the temporary directory. This currently
works as follows:

  * When a fresh package is accessed, its name is entered at the
    beginning of the window

  * Every N seconds, a thread is woken up and removes all packages
    that have fallen off the end of the window.

Obviously, care must be taken when modifying the shared data structures during
both of these operations.
